From c84f2343275dd800a4234ad5b89c0744a0db7433 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:19:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] UICommon: Gen 3 team-editor logic ported from the Android
 build

Port the validated Android Kotlin Gen 3 code (features/xdnetplay/gen3/)
to pure C++ in UICommon/XDNetplay, with no Qt or Android dependencies:

- Gen3Save: the Emerald 128 KiB flash layout - two 57344-byte blocks of
  14 rotating 4096-byte sections, footer at +0x0FF4 (id / checksum /
  signature 0x08012025 / save index), active-block selection by highest
  fully-valid save index, and the per-section checksum with the
  empirically confirmed per-section data-length table. Trainer info
  (section 0) and party (section 1) accessors. Verified-write
  discipline mirroring the validated injectors: re-parse the edited
  image and check every checksum, write to a .tmp, read it back
  byte-identical, back up the existing file to .bak, then rename into
  place.
- Gen3Mon: the 100-byte party struct - PID/OTID header, four 12-byte
  substructures ordered by PID % 24 and XOR-encrypted with PID ^ OTID,
  u16 substructure checksum over the decrypted block, IV/egg/ability
  bitfield, and the party-only stats tail. Decode verifies the
  checksum; encode/decode round-trips byte-identically.
- Gen3Text: the Gen 3 western charset (0xFF-terminated fixed-width
  strings) with UTF-8 conversion for the non-ASCII glyphs.
- Gen3Data: the bundled gen3data.json (species/moves/items/abilities/
  natures/exp tables) loaded with picojson, with normalized-name
  lookups and exp-for-level.
- MonFactory: deterministic PID search satisfying nature, ability
  slot, gender and shininess in priority order (shiny relaxed first,
  bounded search); the Gen 3 stat formula including nature multipliers
  and the Shedinja special case; the Showdown-to-Gen3 EV/IV order
  remap; Hidden Power suffix stripping; the Emerald origins word; and
  the injector's defaults (English, friendship 70, PP 35, Poke Ball).
- ShowdownParser: the full Showdown team-export parser (nickname /
  species / gender / item header, Ability/Level/Shiny/EVs/IVs/Nature
  lines, move list, unknown lines ignored, === headers skipped).

Bundle Data/Sys/XDNetplay/gen3data.json (the same generated data file
the Android build ships as an asset) so the desktop team editor reads
identical game data.

Round-trip verified against the bundled EMERALD-2.sav template: parse,
re-encode the party in place, byte-identical output, all 28 section
checksums and every substructure checksum intact, and a Showdown-built
team injected and re-decoded field-identically.
